> I've tried looking in the sys directory and in the win directory. 
> Specifically, I've looked at wintty.c, getline.c, all of the files in
> sys/unix, etc.  I can't find out anything about how it works.
> 
> I know I could find a library to do it for me, but I know Java and I
> know all about the power of libraries.  Now I want to find out how
> it's done for myself.

NetHack uses termcap (or equivalent functions for another library).
These functions are of the form "what string would I write to move
the cursor to (20,5)" and "how many columns does the screen have".
This is as low level as it is possible to get in a console-mode
program and still support the full range of terminals. If you were
to write the output code today, you would use some variant of
curses, which is a library that wraps around termcap and instead
has functions of the form "move the cursor to (x,y) and print C",
which is much easier to follow.

